{
 "about": "The portraits of player characters and party members, cut from the matrices in assets/pcs (each 3x3: a class or general type to a column, human, elf and dwarf by row, men and women across the two sheets of each set; the two catfolk sheets are all catfolk and the two birdfolk sheets all birdfolk, a calling to each cell in the same order, warrior, mage and cleric; thief, bard and ranger; monk, commoner and aristocrat). Each was looked at before use: class, ancestry and presentation are what the portrait shows, not what the sheet was labelled, and notes say what is in the crop and any doubt. face is where the face sits in the cell's opening, as looked at (fractions of its width and height); crop is the square cut from the sheet and at where the face sits in it (fractions of its side, across and down), both written by python3 scripts/pc-portraits.py, which cuts the copies the game shows (see CompanyPortraits).",
